A few days later. In the underpass at Tokyo Jujutsu High, a routine errand takes a sharp turn when Aoi Todo, a boisterous Grade 1 sorcerer from Kyoto, and Yūmiko Zenin arrive. Todo immediately takes an interest in James, challenging him with an unexpected and seemingly random question: "What’s your kind of girl?" James, never one to back down, answers with a confident grin, proudly declaring his love for his girlfriend, Yūmiko, despite her quirks. Todo is clearly entertained by this and instantly takes a liking to James, bonding over their shared appreciation for strength, competition, and their unconventional personalities.

Todo, curious to see if Megumi can live up to the same standard as Yuta and Hakari, turns his attention to the stoic first-year. When Megumi gives a dull answer to Todo’s question about his type, Todo responds with his signature tough-love approach—knocking Megumi out cold with a single blow. Nobara, furious on Megumi’s behalf, is about to intervene, but Yūmiko Zenin holds her back, knowing this is just Todo’s way of testing strength. Yūmiko herself wants to haze Nobara, insulting and taunting her.

James, seeing his ally down, steps up to protect Megumi, challenging Todo to a fight. He steps into the underpass with a grin, confident in his abilities but aware of Todo’s superior strength. Todo, thrilled by the challenge, accepts, and the two engage in a fierce but friendly battle. James uses his agility and evasive techniques to counter Todo’s overwhelming strength, landing a few solid hits, but Todo ultimately proves his dominance by knocking James into the roof of the underpass. The fight ends with mutual respect, each recognizing the other’s power.

When Panda, Maki, and Toge arrive, they find the two men standing together, grinning like old friends. James, still in high spirits, jokes about the late arrival of his friends and casually mentions that he and Todo are now “bros.” Megumi, though grateful for James stepping in, quietly expresses his desire to handle things on his own, but James reassures him that they’re in this together.

In the end, what started as a random encounter became a moment of bonding between James and Todo, founded on their shared love of competition, strength, and respect. The fight not only forged a connection between them but also helped James feel a little less burdened by the loss of Yuji, as he realized he was starting to build new relationships in the unpredictable world of Jujutsu sorcery.
This is the first time James and Todo meet each other, and they are very happy it happened.
Meanwhile Yuji is still alive in secret and continuing his training and as in canon starting his arc with Nanami, Mahito and Junpei.
The chapter ends with James in high spirits and deeper relationships, he is progressing his technique and starting to live up to his massive potential. he has grown with Yumiko and Kimiko and helped them sort out their issues a bit but Kimiko still poses a potential threat and liability that he needs to monitor.

Chapter 7 Summary:
1. Prologue & Setup:
Timeframe: A week before the Goodwill Event, Yuji and Nanami are secretly hunting Mahito (Yuji is still “dead” in the jujutsu world).
2. Kimiko’s Week of Night Escapades:
Kimiko overpowers the stabilizing bracelet and uses Yumiko’s body to sneak out into Tokyo’s nightlife: indulging in chaos, charming drinks off lonely salarymen (and salarywomen), “borrowing” jewels and dresses, indulging her psychopathic whims, etc. Eventually, she feels and tracks Mahito’s cursed-energy signature to the movie theater murders.
2. James’s Parallel Investigation
James’s discovery: He learns Yumiko has been acting strangely, feeling tired. James hear rumors of a curse user and coupled with Yumikos strange behavior, figures it must be Kimiko. He traces her trail into Tokyo, and also ends up at the theater that same night, confronting the aftermath of Mahito’s attack. 
Theater break-in: James breaks into the cursed movie theater where Mahito slaughtered three bullies. Armed with Dante the carbine, he feels Mahito’s energy but finds only empty, blood-spattered seats and a sleepy attendant.
Security footage: He checks the footage—sees Yuji (not dead) and Nanami investigating. Fury, confusion, and hope collide in his mind.
3. Their Convergence 
Both James and Kimiko independently arrive at the theater, realize they’re on the same trail, and follow the cursed scent together toward Junpei Yoshino’s home. James catches up, they flirt on the way, and Kimiko teases James into thinking about a kiss—until he gently forces Yumiko back in control. Now is not the time for flirtatious games but he was sorely tempted. Back in the body, Yumiko jokingly laments her sister’s choice of heels and bloodstained dress.
4. Arrival at Junpei’s
They reach the Yoshino apartment, sense Yuji’s energy inside, and James wrestles with shock and hope.
5. Reunion & Introductions
A heartfelt but shaky reunion: James meets a living Yuji, Junpei introduces himself, and Yumiko’s dual nature is revealed.
7. Gojo’s Arrival
James calls Gojo; Gojo teleports in his pajamas, apologizes for faking Yuji’s death, reminds James that in war logic must win over feelings, then departs—leaving the four teenagers to bond.
8. James’s Midnight Walk
At 4 AM, James can’t sleep, goes out for a cigarette, and while he’s gone Kenjaku plants the Sukuna finger in Junpei’s apartment.
9. Morning Farewells
After two hours’ sleep, at 7 AM, James, Yumiko, and Yuji leave to rejoin Nanami—still unaware that Junpei’s mother has been killed. They say awkward goodbyes to Junpei.
10. Junpei’s Tragedy
Junpei wakes and cleans up the apartment, finds his murdered mother severed in half by a curse attracted by Sukuna's finger, and breaks down—torn between calling Yuji or Mahito.
11. Junpei’s Despair
Overcome by rage and grief, Junpei chooses vengeance and calls Mahito, setting the stage for the next confrontation. Mahito’s manipulation: Mahito, in league with Kenjaku, comforts Junpei in a twisted parody of fatherhood, planting the idea that Junpei’s bullies framed him—and gives Junpei a cursed technique.
12. James meets Nanami
10:00 AM – The kids meet Nanami after arriving via train. Nanami is furious at: Yuji for breaking protocol and hanging out with Junpei. James for being a loose cannon. Yumiko/Kimiko's existence, which he deems too unstable for fieldwork.
James defends himself and Yumiko, arguing they’d know if Kimiko were in control. He also vents frustration at Nanami for helping keep Yuji’s survival secret from him. Yuji and Yumiko are clearly chastised and embarrassed. Despite tension, they re-focus on the mission: stopping Mahito.
13. Bad news
11:00 AM – Nanami receives a call from Ijichi. He found Junpei’s mom dead in the apartment. Junpei is gone. The news hits hard—Yuji, Yumiko, and James all react with guilt. They were just there. James regains focus and rallies the group: they can’t let things spiral further.
The team splits: Nanami returns to the location of last night’s fight with Mahito. The kids head to Junpei’s school.
14. Confrontation ~11:30 AM – School Ceremony setting: Chaos Begins. James, Yuji, and Yumiko arrive at Satozakura High just as Junpei walks on stage in the auditorium to confront his bully. His poison-cloud jellyfish shikigami knock out students.
Mahito and Kenjaku observe from the rooftop. Mahito drops a veil over the school: no one in, no one out, and no one can see inside.
15. Kids split up
Yuji runs inside to confront Junpei. Yumiko begins evacuating civilians, pushing unconscious students and staff out with gentle shadow waves. James starts ascending the building using superposed vibrational bursts. His goal: reach Mahito and Kenjaku on the roof.


16. James meets Kenjaku
James tears across rooftops to intercept. James reaches the rooftop: Mahito leaves with a promise from Kenjaku: he will fight James for 5 minutes.  First face-off: Kenjaku, in Suguru Geto’s body, greets him with devious calm, dropping cryptic lines about “pieces of the puzzle,” “variables,” and his centuries-long schemes. Kenjaku stalls James by throwing mid-level curses at him while monologuing.
Kenjaku reveals: He planted the cursed finger that killed Junpei’s mom. James figures also orchestrated the one that led to Yuji’s original death. James grows angrier with each passing moment, slowly evolving his power mid-fight. Kenjaku remains smugly fascinated, intrigued by James's growth and resolve. After James finally lands a solid hit, Kenjaku declares time’s up and disappears off the rooftop, smugly avoiding real danger. Note: James does not yet recognize Geto's body or the body-hopping technique. He assumes Kenjaku is a powerful summoner or curse user.
17. Yuji and Junpei clash
Meanwhile – Yuji vs Junpei (Inside the School). Yuji confronts Junpei in the auditorium just as Junpei stabs his bully. Junpei releases poison gas, knocking out most of the students.
They argue: Junpei repeats Mahito’s nihilistic beliefs—people are evil, no hearts. Yuji emotionally fights back—“You’re using your feelings to justify murder.” Reminds Junpei of his mother and what she would want. The two fight across the school, damaging walls and halls. At the same time. 
Junpei bashes Yuji through walls and windows, Yuji begging him to remember his mother’s hopes, arguing the worth of every life. Yuji holds back from actually hurting Junpei.
Evacuation: Yumiko directs shadow platforms to carry unconscious students out.
18. Junpei’s breakdown
Yuji and Junpei end up near a staircase on the second floor. Yuji makes a bold move—lets himself get stabbed to shock Junpei out of his rage. Poisonous tentacles stab Yuji. In torment and grief, Junpei nearly snaps. Junpei falters. He cries. He’s close to giving up revenge. Yuji promises him a way out—he can come to Jujutsu Tech, meet powerful and kind people like James and himself.
19. Enter Mahito
Mahito Descends – Tension Builds. Mahito enters the school from the roof, descending with intent.  As Junpei teeters on redemption, they hear clapping and footsteps. Mahito descends the stairs, mocking them. “The Oscar goes to Itadori, ladies and gentlemen!”. Yuji doesn’t immediately recognize Mahito, but the pieces start coming together. James and Nanami’s previous descriptions begin to click into place. Mahito Reveals Himself to Yuji. Mahito greets Yuji: “Vessel of Sukuna, how nice to meet you properly.” Yuji recognizes the voice and patchwork face from James and Nanami’s descriptions—his eyes widen in horror.
Mahito is giddy over the dramatic tension. Junpei sits awkwardly between them, not grasping the danger. Junpei still thinks Mahito is his friend and defends him verbally.
20. Junpei’s Tragic End (As in Canon)
Mahito enlarges his arm and slams Yuji into a wall, pinning him with brutal force. Junpei shouts at Mahito in confusion and fear. With chilling calm, Mahito steps behind Junpei and puts a “reassuring” hand on his shoulder. He uses Idle Transfiguration and mutates Junpei into a grotesque, gremlin-like creature. The twisted Junpei attacks Yuji, causing no real harm, all while crying and begging. Yuji is shattered. He can’t bring himself to kill Junpei, even in this state.
21. Enter James – Divergence from Canon
James smashes through a window beside Yuji. He kicks Mahito, sending the curse flying and catching him off guard. Though James can’t see souls, he’s trained to sense and attack them due to working with Yumiko and Yuji. His superposed vibrations and Plausible Anomaly twist fate in his favor. Mahito slams into a wall, dazed. James rallies Yuji while Junpei’s broken body begins to deteriorate and leak blood.
Furious beyond reason, James snarls at Mahito: “YOU HAD NO RIGHT.” Mahito mocks James’s anger, but James doesn’t bite—he immediately resumes the assault. Gun forgotten, James begins wailing on Mahito, beating him through the wall and into the courtyard.
22. Mahito Adjusts – Courtyard Battle Begins
Mahito’s laugh falters—he realizes James is a real threat and doesnt care about his taunting. He starts experimenting with his body structure to counter James's attacks. Back in the auditorium, Yumiko finishes evacuating most civilians and starts attacking the veil from inside. Outside, Nanami begins cracking it too. The veil weakens—sunlight starts to break in.
23. Mahito Responds to Sunlight – Human Husk Horde
Seeing the incoming light, Mahito spits out dried human husks and quickly transfigures them into a horde. The husks charge toward civilians and the sorcerers trying to breach the veil. In response, James lands a full-power, maximum-resonance tornado kick, smashing Mahito into the courtyard wall.
24. Yuji and Junpei’s Final Moment
Yuji, covered in blood, holds Junpei in his final moments. Junpei’s skin sloughs off his flesh as he dies a miserable, agonizing death.
25. Three-Way Battle Escalates
Mahito now starts matching James’s rhythm and power, getting a read on his fighting style. . Yuji overcomes his shock and grief and leaps into the courtyard to help James. Mahito begins to panic—Yuji and James together are too much.
Nanami and Yumiko fight off the transfigured humans, protecting civilians.


26. James & Yuji Tag Team – Mahito Pressured
James taunts Mahito: “Aren’t you supposed to be a curse? Born from millennia of humanity’s hatred? You’ll die like you lived: an afterthought.”
Mahito tries to destabilize them: He sends squirming, transfigured homunculi toward Yuji, hoping he can’t bring himself to kill them. Yuji jumps to an awning to avoid them. The creatures can’t hurt him—but emotionally, they weigh heavy. James and Mahito go blow for blow—perfectly matched. James calls it out: “You can’t even kill one man? How embarrassing.”
27. Trap & Turning Point
Mahito lays a fleshy land mine—James steps on it. It pierces his leg, reducing his speed. Painful, but not lethal. Nanami finally clears the remaining husks and leaves Yumiko to protect civilians.
Three things happen at once:
1. James is thrown into a wall, Mahito pinning him with a transfigured, bladed arm. 2. Yuji finally kills the pitiful homunculi, understanding they were already dead—letting them suffer would be cruel. 3. James considers self-sacrifice—he prepares to use his cursed technique to create an explosion by superpositioning millions of slight variations of himself at once.
28. Kimiko Takes the Stage
After clearing civilians and wiping out hemunculi, Yumiko sees James pinned, on the verge of sacrificing himself. Without hesitation, she lets Kimiko out. Yumiko succumbs to Kimiko’s urge—her eyes glow ruby-red, she orders, “Save him…,” and Kimiko seizes control.
.
29. The Queen of Cruelty Descends
Nanami hesitates, caught off-guard as Kimiko launches herself across the courtyard. She radiates cold light, glowing like a divine executioner, ribbons of plasma-like energy trailing her. Ribbons of pure, glass-hard light carve through his flesh. She taunts and slices him limb from limb.
Kimiko is laughing with psychotic delight. Her light burns his flesh, her precision surgical, her intent sadistic. Mahito is immediately on the defensive, limbs contorting wildly to avoid contact. Yuji joins the fray, but his blows are ineffective—Kimiko is overwhelming Mahito alone. As Mahito burns, Kimiko giggles: “Little freak touched MY soul. I should peel yours open like a rotten fruit.” Mahito begins hopping and twitching, pain wracking his body with every touch of her light. He is close to tears.
30. Mockery and Meltdown
Kimiko continues her relentless verbal assault:  “Dance for me, monkey.” Mahito feels something unfamiliar: shame. Kenjaku, watching from a rooftop, narrows his eyes. He doesn’t want Mahito to die—not yet.
31. Mahito's Desperation – Domain Expansion
Driven by pain and panic, Mahito forcibly expands his domain for the first time. A black sphere of warped flesh and bone surrounds him and Kimiko. Mahito activates Self-Embodiment of Perfection. Inside, Kimiko and Mahito slug it out—he tries to dominate her soul, but her sharpened will inflicts pain on him instead. James screams and punches the outside of the barrier in pure panic. Yuji and Nanami join him, all three trying to break in.
32. Inside the Domain – Mahito's Hell
Mahito’s sure-hit technique fails—Kimiko is too alien, her soul fragmented and unnatural. Every time he tries to manipulate her, he gets hurt instead. Fatigue, emotion, and lack of discipline compound the failure. Kimiko laughs, victorious in soul combat: “Aww sweetheart... big technique fail. Bit embarrassing, isn’t it?”. Her words cut deeper than her light.

33. Verbal Evisceration
“You call this a domain? Looks like an orphanage for failed anatomy projects...” “Oh, wait…. That makes sense. Probably reminds you of home, right?” Kimiko mocks. Mahito screeches, losing composure:  “SHUT UP YOU STUCK-UP LITTLE BITCH!”. Kimiko wheezes with glee: “Awww... did I hit a nerve? Don’t worry. You won’t live long enough to regret this pathetic excuse of a fight.” 
Mahito is psychologically unravelling.
34. Enter Sukuna
Yuji smashes through the roof of the barrier, causing it to shudder. Mahito, in his domain, touches Yuji’s soul—and touches Sukuna’s as well.
35. Sukuna’s Domain – Divine Humiliation 
Cut to Sukuna’s innate domain, the spiritual manifestation of his soul and will—a throne of skulls atop a mountain of corpses.
Sukuna is doubled over, laughing hysterically. “I havent laughed this hard in centuries”
He mocks Mahito: “You’re uglier on the inside than the outside. You’re a cockroach playing god.”
He expresses actual respect for Kimiko:  “That girl? She’s got style. And she made you cry? That’s art.”
Sukuna slashes Mahito’s soul, the attack devastating and instant. Mahito’s domain collapses. He falls to the ground, coughing blood.
36. Shame and Salvation
Broken and crawling: Mahito, reduced to tears and begging, tries to crawl away. James, Yuji, and Kimiko tower over him, ready to finish him. Mahito is crying, sobbing like a wounded animal. He tries to crawl away, utterly broken. Kimiko is smug, her victory complete. James is seething, fists clenched and ready to end it.  

37. Kenjaku’s extraction 
Kenjaku intervenes. He sends a flying bird-like curse that swoops down and rescues Mahito, plucking him up mid-crawl. The shame is complete—Mahito, a proud curse, had to be rescued by a human. “You embarrassed yourself… but you’re useful” and they vanishes into the sky—Mahito left whimpering at his rescuer.

38. Battlefield Silence
The courtyard is a smoldering wreck. Burnt walls. Craters. Bloodstains. The distant whine of sirens. The veil fades away. James collapses to one knee, breathing heavily. His wounded leg finally gives out. Yuji drops to both knees, silent tears becoming guttural sobs, hands clutching the pavement. 
Kimiko and Yumiko are floating, mid-air and mid-argument.
“I handled that flawlessly.” “You traumatized a whole building, you sociopath!” “You're just jealous I got to hurt the creepy balloon boy!”
39. Human Fragility, Jujutsu Style
James attempts to push himself up, eyes locked on the fracturing Yumiko. Kimiko and Yumiko’s argument escalates—until James stumbles forward and kisses them mid-float. Their body freezes. Eyes go wide. Floating ceases. The kiss ends. She blinks, then smiles faintly. For a moment, everything’s okay. They survived.
Nanami places a steadying hand on Yuji’s shoulder.
40. Professional Resignation
Nanami pulls out his phone with the tired motion of a man who needs a raise:  “You don’t pay me enough for this, Gojo.”
On the ground, Yuji pounds the pavement, his voice cracking: “IT’S NOT FAIR!!”
41. Emotional Fallout
Yuji and Yumiko, deeply empathetic, are wracked with guilt over Junpei’s death. James, coldly pragmatic, just feels his hatred solidify—Kenjaku is now a target.
"I didn’t know him well. But someone made me care. That’s enough."
42. Gojo Appears – Whiplash Ensues
Gojo’s entrance: With a silent shift, Gojo appears, jangles convenience-store bags (“Whoooo’s hungry?”). He strolls into the chaos like he just stepped off a runway, humming.
He surveys the damage, offers a dramatic sigh of mock sorrow. He holds up a plastic bag of 7-Eleven snacks and sushi like divine offerings: “Remedy for trauma: carbs, salt, and sugar. Works 83% of the time.”
Nanami reflects as he walks off, three kids of special-grade potential, far beyond the ranking system’s scope. He nearly smirks, proud of their strength. Nanami walks away silently, the human embodiment of  "I'm too old for this".
43. Healing in Pieces
James limps over with Yumiko, hand slipping into hers. She squeezes it back tightly—she’s shaking, but she’s there.
Yuji sniffles, still trembling as Gojo offers him sushi. He takes it reluctantly. A bite. Then another. Within moments, he’s quietly munching, a shaky peace settling over him.
44. The Quietest Victory
Gojo sits down beside them, mask off, voice softer: “You did well. All of you. You’re alive. That matters.”
He watches James and Yumiko out of the corner of his eye and for a moment, sees Riko and Geto in their place. it hurts more than he lets on.


45. Normalcy Creeps Back 
James and Yuji bicker, tired but alive: James: “Tuna? Really?” Yuji: “It’s the best one—don’t start, man.” James: “You’re disgusting. Give me the salmon.” For a brief instant, they’re just kids again. The world, broken and cruel as it is, begins to turn normally once more.
46. Intimate Epilogue: James & Yumiko/Kimiko
Rooftop confession: Later, under moonlight, Yumiko asks, “Was it me or her you kissed?” James admits: “I didn’t know who was in control— I kissed you, all of you.” Kimiko’s validation: Kimiko quietly delights—“Haha, he kissed me.” Yumiko’s turmoil: Feeling jealousy of herself, guilt, and relief that James truly accepts both halves. Shared embrace: James hugs them both in a steady, protective embrace. Yumiko melts into him. Kimiko’s ice cracks into genuine vulnerability. 
Gojo watches, heart twinging in silent pride.

47. Gojo's musings

Gojo sees James, Yuji and Megumi as his little bros. Strong enough to understand his humanity, human enough themselves to be his friends.



Chapter 8 Ideas:
James formulates a binding vow to stabilize Yumiko and Kimiko.

Cleanup & Consequences Arc (Immediate aftermath): 
Gakuganji is furious—not about Junpei’s death, but that Yuji, James, and Yumiko disobeyed direct orders and revealed their full powers unsanctioned. Gojo defends them (half-jokingly, half-serious), but tensions in the higher-ups rise. Mei Mei, hearing about Kimiko’s presence, becomes curious and subtly starts sniffing around for profit. Nanami files a report giving Yuji and James unusually high marks—saying they acted beyond their years. Yuji is recommended for "grief counseling" (which in JJK is just being thrown back into the field).

Emotional growth for the kids: Yuji cracks fewer jokes and becomes more quiet. Haunted by Junpei dying grotesquely in his arm. He trains more obsessively now. Yumiko feels unstable, unsure where she ends and Kimiko begins. James is low-key trying to hold everyone together, but also becoming a bit more ruthless, internalizing Kenjaku’s tactics to fight smarter.

Seeds of Future Conflict Arc: Kenjaku Watches After Mahito’s failure, Kenjaku is... amused. This wasn’t about victory—it was about measuring potential. He now sees James and Kimiko as wild variables, unpredictable and dangerous. Plans begin forming around neutralizing or twisting them. He begins subtly laying traps in the background—emotional ones, like targeting Yumiko’s fractured psyche. 
Mahito’s Recovery: Humiliated, injured, and traumatized, Mahito goes into hiding. He becomes more cunning, less playful. His next appearance will be far worse. 

Relationship Tension Arc:

James & Yumiko: Kimiko begins asserting herself more, sometimes speaking uninvited. Yumiko fears James will grow to prefer Kimiko—more confident, more powerful, more like him. James, meanwhile, struggles with guilt: Is he falling for both? Is that betrayal?

Yuji & James: Their bond deepens. Yuji starts seeing James like an older brother, but he’s also scared of him now—James is too okay with killing. James sees Yuji’s softness as both beautiful and a weakness the world will crush.

Kimiko's Secret Agenda:
Kimiko is playing her own long game. She doesn’t want to be “fixed.” She wants the world to bend to her existence. She begins communicating with someone else in secret—perhaps Uraume, intrigued by her concept of duality.

Festival & Bonds: 
A small breather arc—Gojo drags the crew to a festival or theme park. The kids try to act normal for a day, but trauma creeps in. Yuji cries watching fireworks. James stands beside him in silence. Kimiko steals a kiss from James at the festival, then reverts to Yumiko before she can react. This haunts them both for different reasons. 

